[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Bounded Ebers-Moll BJT and junction-storage requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-STORAGE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Explicit charge-only junction companion
STATEMENT: >>>
The simulator shall provide a validated charge-only junction profile whose effective saturation-current scale participates only in transport Q and dQ/dV, with exactly zero static F and dF/dV. It shall share the qualified SPICE depletion/diffusion charge law and accepted BE charge history, expose true displacement current, and not be classified as a DC conduction path. It shall preserve diode/constant-capacitance behavior and retain explicit unavailable energy evidence.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: JunctionStorage in native circuit/model/compile, shared newton/ac/API/audit loops, typed Client DTO. Verification: tests/junction_storage.rs DC-zero, complex AC and BE-KCL; existing diode and constant-C regressions; source-controlled Ebers-Moll composition and native oracle. Three meaningful RED tests failed on unknown old wire tag, then passed after implementation.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-BJT-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Genuine bounded Ebers-Moll current and charge composition
STATEMENT: >>>
The generated frontend shall lower qualified three-terminal NPN/PNP profiles to native conduction-only IS/BF and IS/BR junction paths with separate zero-voltage current senses, BF/BR transport CCCS contributions, and parallel BE/BC charge-only companions using effective IS and TF/TR. Charge shall not flow through or be amplified by the conduction senses. An outer zero-voltage collector sense shall expose signed total collector current. Private nodes shall not become source-name mappings.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Qualified first terms: IS,BF,BR,NF,NR,CJE,VJE,MJE,CJC,VJC,MJC,FC,TF,TR, TNOM27 and LEVEL1. Unsupported terms and instance parameters refuse atomically. The bounded explicit substrate terminal follows SEMI-BJT-SUBSTRATE-001. The later VAF-only extension and shared charge/history contract are specified in BJT-EARLY-CHARGE-001 and BJT-EARLY-HISTORY-001. High-injection, reverse Early, leakage, variable base resistance, temperature and excess-phase couplings remain open; fixed RB/RC/RE are explicit series topology. These absent-coupling defaults reduce to Ebers-Moll; this is not general GP qualification. Implementation: BjtPreparation.cs plus additive Q bridge/readiness. Verification: BjtTests and BjtNativeOracleIntegration; separate provider outcomes retained.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-BJT-SUBSTRATE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Explicit default BJT substrate terminal
STATEMENT: >>>
With an explicit fourth terminal on the bounded NPN or PNP profile, the frontend shall retain the default 1 pS substrate path to the intrinsic collector for NPN and base for PNP. Unsupported substrate conduction terms shall refuse preparation. Storage follows SEMI-BJT-SUBSTRATE-002. The three-terminal composition remains the separately qualified contract of SEMI-BJT-001.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: BjtPreparation and OperatingPointBridge. Verification: BjtTests.Explicit_substrate_uses_default_native_leakage_reference. Native ngspice-47+ reference: BJTsetup defaults vertical NPN and lateral PNP with zero substrate capacitance and saturation current, and BJTload applies the circuit default Gmin across that junction.
<<<

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Qualification investigation: the initial50ps BE grid missed the declared3mV early collector-voltage bound by4.968mV on an owned NPN circuit. At10ps the discrepancy reduced to0.983mV; at2ps early-slice refinement it reduced to0.184mV, consistent with first-order time discretization. The original failed run and fixed bounds remain in local artifacts. The initial Faer AC refusal was retained and referred to the numerical-provider owner. After importing06e8a6b (local47b9809), both LU and Faer passed the original NPN/PNP DC, complex AC and10ps BE comparisons, including signed collector currents and formal coarse/fine error reduction. The unchanged complex residual acceptance is independently qualified by the provider regression. This finite subset does not establish full Gummel-Poon or arbitrary timestep accuracy.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-BJT-SERIES-R-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Constant level-1 BJT terminal resistance
STATEMENT: >>>
The bounded unit-area level-1 profile shall stamp nonnegative model RB, RC and RE in ohms between external and intrinsic terminals. Zero shall preserve the original node allocation. Conduction, substrate reference and junction charge shall use the intrinsic terminals, and the collector observable shall retain total external current. Current-dependent base resistance parameters and a positive resistance with unrepresentable conductance shall refuse.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification uses BjtTests and compat/ngspice/bjt-ohmic-resistance.cir. Ngspice bjttemp.c assigns RBM=RB when RBM is omitted. The retained default and tight reference sweep results are separate.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SEMI-BJT-SUBSTRATE-002
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Nominal level-1 BJT substrate depletion charge
STATEMENT: >>>
For the bounded unit-area 27 C NPN and PNP profiles, the frontend shall map CJS, VJS and MJS and their CCS/CSUB, PS and MS aliases to a charge-only substrate junction. Aliases shall share duplicate detection. The junction voltage is the substrate potential minus the intrinsic collector potential for NPN or the intrinsic base potential for PNP. An omitted substrate terminal uses ground for charge. A zero capacitance or coincident terminals shall require no charge element. The depletion law shall transition at zero junction voltage with continuous charge and capacitance. Invalid parameter domains and unsupported substrate conduction shall refuse preparation.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: BjtPreparation.cs reuses native JunctionStorage with zero forward coefficient and transport time. Verification: BjtTests checks explicit and omitted ports, intrinsic nodes with terminal resistance, aliases and malformed model cards. BjtNativeOracleIntegration compares nominal grounded-substrate NPN/PNP DC, complex AC and transient at both LU and Faer entry points. Scope excludes substrate conduction, nonnominal temperature, nondefault area, full Gummel-Poon and sensitivity.
<<<

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Substrate qualification on Windows at baseline e9c3936 with the SEMI-BJT-SUBSTRATE-002 changes: dotnet test dotnet/Simulator.Frontend.Tests --filter FullyQualifiedName~Bjt --collect "XPlat Code Coverage" ran 46 tests, zero failures and zero skips on SDK 10.0.403. Artifacts, grammar and test output were isolated under E:/Artifacts/Spice-bjt-substrate-e9c3936. The grounded-substrate oracle exercises both polarities on LU and Faer, at DC, 10 MHz complex AC and four transient checkpoints through 100 ns. The fine BE grid is 10 ps. Bounds are 0.2 uV and 0.2 nA for DC, 20 uV and 20 nA per AC component, and 3 mV and 2 uA for transient checkpoints. The reference is ngspice 47+ (SHA-256 12BC57018AA5142D28065704D09BC6B06DA2A3886F7864CA042ED4824CCF910F), driven with first-order Gear for transient. Native binary SHA-256 4F915B77C4CD28ADF76D6EAC8B7845168C0A27723FC4A8385E1865041A82F582. Frontend Coverlet class line/branch percentages were PreparedBjt 100/97.61 and BjtPreparation 97.72/88.79. All four topology cases caught an intentional substrate polarity reversal. After restoration nine focused tests passed. This run did not measure native coverage or run a fuzz/property campaign. The original RSpice diffpair deck also needs Early effect and its requested transfer-function and sensitivity analyses.
<<<
